---
import FilaLayout from '../../layouts/FilaLayout.astro';
import ElSegundoLookbook from '../../components/fila/ElSegundoLookbook.astro';
import {CHAPTERS, CREATED_AT, INDEPENDENT_LABEL, SOURCES} from '../../data/fila-el-segundo';
const hero = '/images/fila-el-segundo/courtyard-hero.webp';
const heroAlt = 'Original AI-generated campaign concept: three fictional adults in cobalt, silver and terracotta sportswear in an imaginary coastal courtyard, with a blue bench and painted court arc.';
const chapterNotes = [
  {id:'coast',number:'01',name:'Ocean',subtitle:'A boundary, not a postcard.',image:'/images/fila-el-segundo/es03-front.webp',reference:'beach',text:'El Segundo’s beach meets a broad Pacific horizon. We translate that horizontal clarity into blue shoulder arcs, sea-glass panels and a collar with one precise edge. The clothes offer an idea of ease; salt, weather and wear still need real testing.'},
  {id:'works',number:'02',name:'Works',subtitle:'Engineering, made gentle.',image:'/images/fila-el-segundo/es04-front.webp',reference:'aerospace',text:'The town has a real aerospace context. Our reading stays at the level of form: offset openings, rectangular panels, repeated ribs and quiet silver. These are everyday garment concepts, with no technical certification or corporate partnership.'},
  {id:'court',number:'03',name:'Court',subtitle:'One more game. Then Main Street.',image:'/images/fila-el-segundo/es08-front.webp',reference:'recreation',text:'Recreation Park is an actual tennis and pickleball place. Downtown gives the day another register. We choose warm pigment, pale pleats and useful pockets to make the transition feel easy. The palette is our interpretation, not a claim about the park’s court paint.'},
];
---
<FilaLayout title="FILA v2 / The El Segundo field collection" description="Nine original independent garment concepts shaped by El Segundo’s coast, aerospace forms and court-to-Main-Street life. Explore views, details and your own afternoon edit." image={hero} imageAlt={heroAlt} imageWidth={1672} imageHeight={941} published={CREATED_AT} modified={CREATED_AT} dataHref="/fila/el-segundo.json" creditsHref="#credits" footerNote="Independent PointCast design concept · researched 3 October 2026.">
  <div class="local-exhibition">
    <section class="local-opening" aria-labelledby="local-title">
      <div class="opening-index"><span>FILA / AN INDEPENDENT STUDY</span><span>VOLUME 02 · EL SEGUNDO · 2027 CONCEPT</span></div>
      <div class="local-heading"><h1 id="local-title"><span>El</span>Segundo<em>.</em></h1><div class="opening-note"><span class="field-stamp" aria-hidden="true">ES<br />V.2</span><p>Ocean on one side.<br />Possibility on the other.</p><p class="opening-dek">A new field collection, imagined for the space between a morning walk, a game and Main Street.</p><a class="enter-link" href="#collection">Explore nine looks <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div>
      <figure class="campaign"><img src={hero} width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high" alt={heroAlt} /><figcaption><span>THE COASTAL COURTYARD / ORIGINAL CAMPAIGN CONCEPT</span><span>AI-generated fictional scene and models. No real venue or event is depicted.</span></figcaption></figure>
      <div class="opening-bottom"><p>{INDEPENDENT_LABEL}</p><a href="/fila/2027/">Explore the original 2027 collection ↗</a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="local-thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title"><p class="eyebrow">THE QUESTION / WHAT MIGHT EL SEGUNDO WEAR?</p><h2 id="thesis-title">Let the town<br />change the <em>line.</em></h2><div><p>Keep the sporting collar, the clean boundary and the confidence of a complete outfit. Give them another setting: a flat blue horizon, a silver working vocabulary, and the unhurried utility of a court day.</p><p>This is a local design reading. Place facts come from civic and institutional sources; the silhouettes, colors and garment proposals are ours. Every image in this chapter was generated afresh.</p></div></section>
    <section class="field-notes" aria-labelledby="field-title"><div class="section-label"><span>FIELD NOTES / THREE REGISTERS</span><span>PLACE → FORM</span></div><h2 id="field-title" class="sr-only">The local references behind the collection</h2>
      {chapterNotes.map(note => <article class={`field-note field-${note.id}`}><div class="field-number" aria-hidden="true">{note.number}</div><figure><img src={note.image} width="768" height="1024" loading="lazy" alt={`Original AI-generated ${note.name} garment concept, front view.`} /><figcaption>Original AI-generated garment concept.</figcaption></figure><div class="field-copy"><p class="eyebrow">{note.name.toUpperCase()} / LOCAL READING</p><h3>{note.subtitle}</h3><p>{note.text}</p><a href={SOURCES.find(source => source.id === note.reference)?.url}>Read the place reference ↗</a><div class="field-palette" aria-label={`${note.name} proposed palette`}>{CHAPTERS.find(chapter => chapter.id === note.id)?.colors.map(color => <span style={`background:${color}`}><span class="sr-only">{color}</span></span>)}</div></div></article>)}
    </section>
    <ElSegundoLookbook />
    <section class="local-afterword" aria-labelledby="after-title"><p class="eyebrow">AFTER THE EDIT / DEVELOP IT IN THE REAL WORLD</p><h2 id="after-title">A good idea<br />has to <em>move.</em></h2><div><p>The next step would be physical: fabric samples, pocket loads, reach, sitting, laundering and a day on court. A rendered seam does not establish a working pattern. These outfits are concepts, not manufactured products or performance claims.</p><p>For RALLY, the lesson is a vocabulary that belongs to a place: a few clear forms, a useful pocket, a color people remember. Develop the needs and fit with local players; create your own assets and identity.</p><a href="/fila/">Return to the FILA heritage exhibition ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="local-sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="source-title"><p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE DESK / VERIFIED 3 OCTOBER 2026</p><h2 id="source-title">Place first.<br /><em>Interpretation follows.</em></h2><p>Official sources establish the local context. The design inferences below are editorial proposals; none of these organizations sponsors the collection.</p><ol>{SOURCES.map(source => <li><a href={source.url}>{source.title} ↗</a><p><strong>Place fact.</strong> {source.fact}</p><p><strong>Our reading.</strong> {source.inference}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
    <section class="local-credits" id="credits" aria-labelledby="credit-title"><p class="eyebrow">IMAGE DESK / NEW ORIGINALS</p><h2 id="credit-title">Imagined garments.<br />Visible provenance.</h2><p>The campaign scene and all nine paired garment renderings are original AI-generated design concepts created for this chapter on 3 October 2026. No historical FILA photograph or original 2027 artwork was used as an image input. Models are fictional; garment front and back are imagined, not verified manufacturing specifications.</p><p>Front and back views are separate crops of each new paired original. Detail views are enlarged crops of its front rendering, not physical material samples. Web assets are optimized derivatives. The <a href="/fila/el-segundo.json">structured collection data</a> includes source links and image provenance.</p><div class="edition-links"><a href="/fila/">01 / Heritage exhibition ↗</a><a href="/fila/2027/">02 / Court, Club, Coast ↗</a><a href="/fila/el-segundo.json">03 / El Segundo data ↗</a></div></section>
  </div>
</FilaLayout>
<style>
  .local-exhibition{--blue:#145fc4;--clay:#b65132;--silver:#b7bec4;--ink:#12283f;overflow:clip}.local-opening{padding:30px var(--gutter) 0}.opening-index{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;font:10px/1.6 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;letter-spacing:.06em}.local-heading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr;align-items:end;gap:4vw;padding:45px 0 35px}.local-heading h1{font-size:clamp(68px,13vw,204px);font-weight:600;line-height:.82;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:0}.local-heading h1>span{display:block;color:var(--blue)}.local-heading h1 em{font-family:Georgia,serif;color:var(--clay);font-weight:400}.opening-note{max-width:36ch;margin-left:auto}.opening-note>p:first-of-type{font:italic clamp(22px,2.5vw,39px)/1.12 Georgia,serif}.opening-dek{font-size:14px;line-height:1.65}.field-stamp{display:block;float:right;margin-left:20px;border:1px solid var(--ink);border-radius:50%;width:65px;height:65px;text-align:center;padding:14px 0;font:12px/1.5 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;transform:rotate(9deg)}.enter-link{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:30px;min-height:48px;border-top:1px solid var(--ink);font:12px/1.5 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;text-decoration:none;margin-top:24px}.enter-link span{font-size:28px}.campaign{margin:0 -2vw}.campaign img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.campaign figcaption{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px;padding:12px 2vw;font:9px/1.6 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace}.campaign figcaption span:last-child{max-width:50ch;text-align:right}.opening-bottom{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:35px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);font:10px/1.7 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;padding:18px 0}.opening-bottom p{margin:0;max-width:70ch}.opening-bottom a{white-space:nowrap}
  .local-thesis,.local-afterword{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:25px 6vw;padding:90px var(--gutter)}.local-thesis>.eyebrow,.local-afterword>.eyebrow{grid-column:1/-1}.local-thesis h2,.local-afterword h2{font-size:clamp(48px,6vw,95px);line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:0}.local-thesis h2 em,.local-afterword h2 em,.local-sources h2 em{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400}.local-thesis>div p,.local-afterword>div p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;max-width:48ch;margin-top:0}.local-afterword{background:var(--blue);color:#f5efdf}.local-afterword :focus-visible{outline-color:#f5efdf}.local-afterword a{font-size:12px}.field-notes{padding:0 var(--gutter) 80px}.field-note{display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px 1fr 1fr;gap:4vw;border-top:1px solid var(--ink);padding:35px 0 45px;align-items:center}.field-number{font:clamp(40px,6vw,100px)/1 Georgia,serif;align-self:start;color:var(--blue)}.field-works .field-number{color:#627180}.field-court .field-number{color:var(--clay)}.field-note figure{background:#e8e2d6;max-width:360px;justify-self:center;width:100%}.field-note figure img{display:block;width:100%;height:430px;object-fit:contain;mix-blend-mode:multiply}.field-note figcaption{font:9px/1.5 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;padding:10px 15px}.field-copy h3{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,60px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:20px 0}.field-copy p:not(.eyebrow){font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;max-width:42ch}.field-copy a{font-size:11px}.field-palette{display:flex;gap:5px;margin-top:24px}.field-palette>span{display:block;width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;border:1px solid #12283f33}.field-notes>.section-label{padding-bottom:25px}
  .local-sources,.local-credits{padding:70px var(--gutter);border-top:1px solid #12283f55}.local-sources h2{font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,78px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:25px 0}.local-sources>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:65ch;font-size:14px}.local-sources ol{list-style:none;counter-reset:refs;padding:20px 0 0;margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:35px 6vw}.local-sources li{counter-increment:refs;border-top:1px solid #12283f66;padding-top:15px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.local-sources li>a{font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;display:block;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}.local-sources li>a:before{content:counter(refs,decimal-leading-zero)' / ';font:10px 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace}.local-sources li p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.75}.local-sources strong{font-weight:600}.local-credits{background:#e3ddd1}.local-credits h2{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,60px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:25px 0}.local-credits>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:85ch;font-size:12px;line-height:1.8}.edition-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;font:10px/1.7 'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;padding-top:20px}.sr-only{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}
  @media(max-width:900px){.local-heading{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.local-heading h1{font-size:12vw}.field-note{grid-template-columns:50px 1fr 1fr;gap:3vw}.field-note figure img{height:360px}.local-thesis,.local-afterword{padding-top:65px;padding-bottom:65px}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.local-opening{padding-top:22px}.opening-index{font-size:8px;display:block}.opening-index span{display:block;margin-bottom:8px}.local-heading{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:25px 0}.local-heading h1{font-size:clamp(68px,17vw,104px)}.opening-note{max-width:none;margin:20px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0 20px}.opening-note .field-stamp{display:none}.opening-note>p:first-of-type{font-size:24px;margin:0}.opening-dek{font-size:11px;margin:0}.enter-link{grid-column:1/-1;margin-top:22px;font-size:11px}.campaign{margin:0 -5vw}.campaign figcaption{display:block;padding:14px 5vw;font-size:8px}.campaign figcaption span{display:block}.campaign figcaption span:last-child{text-align:left;max-width:none;margin-top:8px}.opening-bottom{display:block;font-size:9px;padding:16px 0}.opening-bottom a{display:block;margin-top:12px;white-space:normal}.local-thesis,.local-afterword{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:50px var(--gutter);gap:20px}.local-thesis h2,.local-afterword h2{font-size:54px}.local-thesis>div p,.local-afterword>div p{font-size:13px}.field-notes{padding-bottom:45px}.field-note{grid-template-columns:30px 1fr;gap:15px;padding:25px 0}.field-number{font-size:35px}.field-note figure{max-width:280px}.field-note figure img{height:350px}.field-copy{grid-column:2}.field-copy h3{font-size:36px;margin:15px 0}.field-copy p:not(.eyebrow){font-size:12px}.field-note figcaption{font-size:8px}.field-palette>span{width:24px;height:24px}.local-sources,.local-credits{padding:45px var(--gutter)}.local-sources ol{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.local-sources h2{font-size:43px}.local-credits h2{font-size:37px}.local-sources>p:not(.eyebrow){font-size:12px}.local-sources li>a{font-size:14px}}
</style>
